      "math_academy_id": "e-4720",
      "problem": "Let ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/foundations/14140373/assets/5b447e40db3ad749fa7d891f52e42bfe31bbb9c719e438809e19b744c71e404c.svg) Find the row operation that, when applied to a $2\\times 2$ matrix $A,$ gives the result of the product $EA.$",
      "worked_solution": "The matrix $E$ is obtained by taking the identity matrix and replacing the second row with the result of adding $5$ times the first row to the second row:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=5{R}_{1}+{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =E\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $EA$ is equivalent to applying the row operation $R_2:=5R_1+ R_2$ to $A.$",
